# 8. UNIFIED TRANSACTION STATUS MANAGEMENT

Implement a backend-controlled status lifecycle.

| Status | Meaning | Included in confirmed balance |
|---|---|---|
| Pending Confirmation | Waiting for recipient | No |
| Confirmed | Accepted or added through valid QR/code | Yes |
| Rejected | Recipient rejected request | No |
| Cancelled | Sender cancelled request | No |
| Partially Settled | Some amount settled | Existing settlement rules |
| Settled | Fully settled | Existing settlement rules |
| Deleted | Durably deleted/hidden according to deletion policy | No |

Important:

- Pending, Rejected and Cancelled must not affect confirmed balances.
- Confirmed transactions must follow existing settlement calculations.
- Preserve existing partially settled and settled transaction logic.
- Do not double-count a shared transaction in the same user's balance.
- Do not modify unrelated financial records.

